{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "October 2026, Microsoft Research announced a complete proof",
      "kind": "date",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E2."
    },
    {
      "text": "First proposed in 1995",
      "kind": "date",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E1."
    },
    {
      "text": "July 2026",
      "kind": "date",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E11."
    },
    {
      "text": "October 1, 2026",
      "kind": "date",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E12."
    },
    {
      "text": "October 4, 2026",
      "kind": "date",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E13."
    },
    {
      "text": "The KLS conjecture asks whether the best flat or hyperplane cut is always nearly as effective as the best cut of any shape for a broad class of high-dimensional probability distributions.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E3."
    },
    {
      "text": "KLS plays a central role in the theory of high-dimensional sampling because the geometry of these cuts governs how quickly random walks can explore a distribution.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E4."
    },
    {
      "text": "human researchers directed the overall discovery loop by constantly evaluating, pruning, and redirecting the AI search space.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E5."
    },
    {
      "text": "AI tools assisted the researchers by exploring candidate approaches, searching sparse search trees, and carrying out detailed symbolic derivations.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E6."
    },
    {
      "text": "The researchers determined the mathematical direction, selected the most promising intermediate ideas, and assembled the final unified argument.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E7."
    },
    {
      "text": "a Lean 4 formalization was subsequently released",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E8."
    },
    {
      "text": "Before this work, the best known result, established in July 2026, allowed that bound to grow slowly as the number of dimensions increased.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E11."
    },
    {
      "text": "In the October 1, 2026 version of the paper, this reduced the dependence on dimension to the iterated logarithm.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E12."
    },
    {
      "text": "This eliminated the dependence on the number of dimensions and completed the proof in the October 4, 2026 version of the paper.",
      "kind": "other",
      "status": "verified",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/solving-a-31-year-old-grand-challenge-in-mathematics-the-kls-conjecture",
      "note": "Supported by E13."
    }
  ]
}
